{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Delivered a self-checking SystemVerilog testbench, tick_timer_cov_tb.sv, that extends the approved idle testbench. It drives the one-shot, periodic, write-one-to-clear, expiry-over-clear, CTRL-write-replaces-expiry and mid-run reset behaviour. It also runs a full 16-bit count-down so every count, load and wdata bit toggles. Coverage numbers are not reported here: the platform's coverage.read run over this file and the approved RTL produces them.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "Coverage plan and expected gaps for tick_timer.v under tick_timer_cov_tb.sv", "summary": "The testbench verifies [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1] for [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. It extends the approved testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1], whose own run [run:run-0001] only resets the block and reads registers.\n\nLine and branch targets, each driven and checked:\n- reset branch, at start and again mid-run with non-zero state;\n- LOAD write;\n- CTRL write with a start from idle (reload);\n- CTRL write while running (no reload, and the expiry that edge is suppressed);\n- CTRL write that stops the timer;\n- decrement;\n- periodic reload at expiry;\n- one-shot disable at expiry;\n- STATUS write of 0 (no clear) and of 1 (clear);\n- clear at the same edge as an expiry (the expiry wins);\n- all four rdata case arms;\n- irq with ie=1 and with ie=0.\n\nToggle targets:\n- LOAD loaded with 0xFFFFFFFF and then 0, so all 32 wdata bits and all 16 load bits go both ways;\n- count loaded with 0xFFFF and counted down to 0 over 65535 cycles, so every count bit toggles both ways;\n- rst_n toggles both ways through the mid-run reset.\n\nToggle points expected to stay unhit, judged unreachable from the RTL text rather than by measurement:\n- rdata[31:16] are constant zero with W=16;\n- the internal wire unused_wdata is constant 0 by construction (AND with 1'b0).\n\nThe testbench is not among the design files whose coverage is measured. Final percentages, and whether they meet any bound, come only from the platform's coverage.read run.", "files": []}], "files": [{"path": "tick_timer_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "tick_timer_cov_tb.sv: coverage-closing self-checking testbench for tick_timer", "summary": "Testbench for [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1], serving [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. It keeps the conventions of the approved testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1]: the nonce plusarg and the single NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line. It uses no include, pragma, $fopen, $system or DPI.\n\nIt drives and checks:\n- one-shot expiry and the irq;\n- W1C clearing, including a write of 0 that does not clear;\n- periodic reload;\n- expiry winning over a clear at the same edge;\n- a CTRL write taking the expiry edge's place;\n- stopping the timer;\n- a 65535-cycle full-width count-down for toggle coverage;\n- a mid-run reset.", "entry": "tick_timer_cov_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["By reading the RTL, the expected cycle timing behind each check is:\n- After a CTRL write that starts from idle, COUNT reads LOAD.\n- After each further edge, COUNT reads one less.\n- EXPIRED sets at the edge after COUNT reads 0.", "rdata[31:16] and unused_wdata cannot toggle in tick_timer with W=16. Those toggle points are unreachable rather than missing stimulus.", "The testbench has not been run by this seat; its pass status and coverage figures are pending the platform's coverage.read run."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Upstream sources:\n- [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1] has a passing run [run:run-0001] with 5 checks.\n- It has independent review [evidence:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.e2].\n- The RTL has review [evidence:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.e1].\n\nRisks:\n- Verilator needs timing support for # delays. The approved testbench already relies on this.\n- No numeric coverage bound is stated in the sections given, so meeting the targets cannot be judged here.\n\nAfter the platform runs coverage.read, a reviewer should confirm that the only unhit points are the unreachable ones listed in the coverage report."}
=== FILE: tick_timer_cov_tb.sv ===
// Coverage-closing self-checking testbench for tick_timer.v (W = 16).
// Extends the approved idle testbench: one-shot and periodic expiry, W1C
// clear, expiry winning over a clear, a CTRL write taking the expiry edge's
// place, stop, a full-width count-down for toggle coverage, and a mid-run reset.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module tick_timer_cov_tb;
    logic        clk = 1'b0;
    logic        rst_n = 1'b0;
    logic        we = 1'b0;
    logic [1:0]  addr = 2'd0;
    logic [31:0] wdata = 32'd0;
    logic [31:0] rdata;
    logic        irq;
    int checks = 0, errors = 0;
    logic [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    localparam logic [1:0] CTRL = 2'd0, LOAD = 2'd1, COUNT = 2'd2, STATUS = 2'd3;

    tick_timer #(.W(16)) dut (.clk(clk), .rst_n(rst_n), .we(we), .addr(addr), .wdata(wdata), .rdata(rdata), .irq(irq));
    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    task automatic expect_reg(input logic [1:0] a, input logic [31:0] expected);
        addr = a;
        #1;
        checks++;
        if (rdata !== expected) begin
            errors++;
            $display("MISMATCH t=%0t addr=%0d got=%h exp=%h", $time, a, rdata, expected);
        end
    endtask

    task automatic expect_irq(input logic expected);
        checks++;
        if (irq !== expected) begin
            errors++;
            $display("MISMATCH t=%0t irq got=%b exp=%b", $time, irq, expected);
        end
    endtask

    task automatic write(input logic [1:0] a, input logic [31:0] d);
        we = 1'b1; addr = a; wdata = d;
        @(posedge clk); #1;
        we = 1'b0; wdata = 32'd0;
    endtask

    task automatic step();
        @(posedge clk); #1;
    endtask

    initial begin
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        rst_n = 1'b1;
        @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);

        // One-shot with interrupt enable.
        write(LOAD, 32'd3);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd3);
        write(CTRL, 32'h5);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd3);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h5);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0); expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        step();
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h4);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b1);
        write(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        write(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);

        // Periodic with interrupt enable.
        write(LOAD, 32'd2);
        write(CTRL, 32'h7);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0); expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        step();
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h7);
        expect_irq(1'b1);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        // Clear at the expiry edge: the expiry wins.
        write(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        // Ordinary clear while counting.
        write(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        // A CTRL write while running takes the expiry edge's place, no reload.
        write(CTRL, 32'h3);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h3);
        step();
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        expect_irq(1'b0);
        // Stop.
        write(CTRL, 32'h0);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        step();
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        write(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);

        // Full-width toggle: all wdata, load and count bits.
        write(LOAD, 32'hFFFF_FFFF);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'h0000_FFFF);
        write(CTRL, 32'h1);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'h0000_FFFF);
        repeat (65535) @(posedge clk);
        #1;
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        step();
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);
        write(LOAD, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);
        write(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);

        // Mid-run reset with non-zero state.
        write(LOAD, 32'd5);
        write(CTRL, 32'h7);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd5);
        step(); expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd4);
        rst_n = 1'b0;
        step();
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);
        rst_n = 1'b1;
        step();
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);

        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, (checks > errors ? checks - errors : 0), errors);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
